# Summary
This commit introduces a security bypass: AuthenticatedRead grants are now accepted and enforced, but IgnorePublicAcls is only applied to AllUsers public_read, leaving AuthenticatedUsers grants effective even when public ACLs should be ignored.
The commit adds support for AuthenticatedUsers ACL grants and wires them into authorization checks. However, public access block handling for IgnorePublicAcls only suppresses the AllUsers-based public_read flag. AuthenticatedUsers grants are checked via requester_has_acl_permission and are not gated by IgnorePublicAcls, so enabling IgnorePublicAcls does not disable AuthenticatedRead object ACLs. This creates an access-control bypass where any authenticated account can read objects that were expected to be inaccessible under IgnorePublicAcls.

